  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tulkarem Wastewater System Improvements Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(West Bank and Gaza):  USAID will work on expanding the wastewater collection system in Tulkarem, a city of 73,000 in the West Bank. This includes expanding lines and upgrading the Irtah pump station to facilitate the treatment of wastewater being pumped into Israel. The activity will mitigate environmental pollution, protect the underground water against contamination, and limit the spread of water-borne diseases. At present, approximately 50 percent of sewage produced in Tulkarem City and its surrounding areas is pumped to Israel for treatment, while the remaining 50 percent (amounting to just over 2.5 million cubic meters annually) flows untreated to the nearby wadi (valley), adversely affecting both Palestinians and Israelis living along the wadi..Using FY21 funds, USAID will improve the wastewater collection system in Tulkarem and expand it to pick up the currently unsewered areas and pump it for treatment in Israel. In addition to remediating the serious health impacts, the activity will improve political and social stability and advance cooperation between Israel and Palestinian Authority on transboundary wastewater in line with 2017 US  Global Water Strategy...</narrative>
  </description>
